{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Sym.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finsupp.Weight","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finsupp.Multiset","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Homogeneous","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L232-L245","doc":"**The label is faithful.** Distinct points of the diagram carry distinct `I₃`, so the\nfour-dimensionality of `quadruplet_dim` is a count of four *isospin-labelled* states and\nnot merely of four basis vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_odd","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L224-L230","doc":"**The weights are half-integral**, i.e. `2I₃` is odd at every point. This is the\nstatement that distinguishes a fermionic multiplet, and it is degree-dependent: at even\ndegree the same construction gives even `2I₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_mem_ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_mem_ladder","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L215-L222","doc":"**The ladder is closed.** Every point of the degree-3 two-flavour diagram carries one\nof the four isospin-3/2 weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_quartetPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3_quartetPoint","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L207-L213","doc":"**The ladder is attained.** `2I₃` on the four diagram points runs `3, 1, -1, -3`.\nTogether with `twoI3_mem_ladder` this makes the value set exactly those four. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.quartetPoint_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.quartetPoint_mem","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L198-L205","doc":"Each `quartetPoint` really is a point of the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.quartetPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.quartetPoint","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L194-L196","doc":"The `k`-th point of the degree-3 two-flavour diagram: `u^(3-k) d^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.twoI3","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L190-L192","doc":"**Twice the third isospin component**, `2I₃ = n_u - n_d`. Doubled so that the\nhalf-integer weights of a fermionic multiplet are integers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.coordSum_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.coordSum_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L184-L188","doc":"A weight-diagram point at two flavours has quark counts summing to the degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.decuplet_ne_quadruplet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.decuplet_ne_quadruplet","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L154-L161","doc":"**The anti-fitting guard, machine-checked.**  The decuplet claim is conditional on `N = 3`:\nthe symmetric channel at `N = 2` is a *different size*. Were the dimension `N`-independent this\nwould fail, which is what makes the conditional a real hypothesis rather than a hedge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.quadruplet_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.quadruplet_dim","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L149-L152","doc":"**The quadruplet.**  The same partition at `N = 2` gives only `C(4,3) = 4`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:delta-quartet-isospin-ladder","label":"prop:delta-quartet-isospin-ladder","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/delta-quartet-isospin-ladder.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.decuplet_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.decuplet_dim","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L144-L147","doc":"**The decuplet.**  `N = 3` flavours, `n = 3` quarks: dimension `C(5,3) = 10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.finrank_homogeneousSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.finrank_homogeneousSubmodule","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L131-L140","doc":"**The dimension formula.**  The space of degree-`n` homogeneous forms in `N` variables — the\n`n`-th symmetric power of the dual of an `N`-dimensional space — has dimension `C(N + n - 1, n)`.\n\nGeneral in `N`, `n` and the base ring — no division is used anywhere, so no field is needed.\nThis is the proposition's mathematical core; everything below is instantiation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.homogeneousSubmodule_eq_restrictSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.homogeneousSubmodule_eq_restrictSupport","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L114-L129","doc":"**The degree-`n` forms are exactly the polynomials supported on the weight diagram.**\n\nThis is the step that turns a counting statement about the diagram into a statement about a\nvector space: `restrictSupport` carries a canonical basis indexed by the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.degree_eq_weight_one'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.degree_eq_weight_one'","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L108-L111","doc":"`Finsupp.degree` is `Finsupp.weight 1`, in the form the homogeneity predicate uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.card_weightDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.card_weightDiagram","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L104-L106","doc":"**Stars and bars.**  The weight diagram has `C(N + n - 1, n)` points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.instFintypeElemFinsuppFinNatWeightDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.instFintypeElemFinsuppFinNatWeightDiagram","kind":"instance","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.wdEquivSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.wdEquivSym","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L90-L100","doc":"**A weight-diagram point is a multiset of `n` flavours.**\n\nThis is the manuscript table's \"Content\" column as a theorem: the state `uds` *is* the multiset\n`{u, d, s}`, and the exponent vector `(1,1,1)` is the same datum written additively. The\nbijection is `Finsupp.toMultiset`, and it is what lets stars and bars count the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.weightDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.SymmetricChannelDimension.weightDiagram","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/SymmetricChannelDimension.lean#L84-L88","doc":"**The weight diagram**: exponent vectors of total degree `n` in `N` flavours.\n\nAt `N = n = 3` these are the quark-count coordinates `(n_u, n_d, n_s)` with\n`n_u + n_d + n_s = 3` — the triangle whose corners are `Δ⁺⁺ (uuu)`, `Δ⁻ (ddd)` and `Ω⁻ (sss)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}